WEBVTT

00:00:00.275 --> 00:00:04.237
Stop it! Can't you see
it's bothering him? Stop it!

00:00:15.957 --> 00:00:18.126
Um....

00:00:21.754 --> 00:00:25.758
Perhaps you could give us the last
Unforgivable Curse, Miss Granger.

00:00:28.094 --> 00:00:29.304
No?

00:00:30.763 --> 00:00:32.891
Avada Kedavra!

00:00:36.644 --> 00:00:38.271
The Killing Curse.

00:00:39.314 --> 00:00:42.400
Only one person is known
to have survived it...

00:00:43.109 --> 00:00:45.320
...and he's sitting in this room.

00:01:06.174 --> 00:01:09.302
[BELL TOLLING]

00:01:17.060 --> 00:01:18.770
RON:
Brilliant, isn't he?

00:01:18.937 --> 00:01:23.024
Completely demented, of course, and
terrifying to be in the same room with...

00:01:23.191 --> 00:01:26.319
...but he's really been there, you know?
He's looked evil in the eye.

00:01:26.402 --> 00:01:29.155
There's a reason those curses
are unforgivable.

00:01:29.322 --> 00:01:33.368
To perform them in a classroom....
I mean, did you see Neville's face?

00:01:36.371 --> 00:01:37.705
Neville?

00:01:37.956 --> 00:01:39.374
Son?

00:01:39.707 --> 00:01:41.376
You all right?

00:01:42.377 --> 00:01:45.713
Come on. We'll have a cup of tea.
I want to show you something.

00:02:00.353 --> 00:02:02.355
GIRL:
We're gonna be late!

00:02:08.403 --> 00:02:10.238
[CHATTERING]

00:02:12.740 --> 00:02:15.243
[APPLAUSE]

00:02:15.827 --> 00:02:18.246
Come on, Cedric. Put it in!

00:02:24.419 --> 00:02:26.379
[APPLAUSE]

00:02:33.761 --> 00:02:36.347
Eternal glory. Be brilliant, wouldn't it?

00:02:36.431 --> 00:02:39.142
Three years from now,
when we're old enough to be chosen.

00:02:39.392 --> 00:02:40.893
Yeah, rather you than me.

00:02:41.102 --> 00:02:43.021
FRED AND GEORGE:
Yes!

00:02:45.273 --> 00:02:47.150
Thank you, thank you.

00:02:47.400 --> 00:02:50.361
-Well, lads, we've done it.
-Cooked it up just this morning.

00:02:50.445 --> 00:02:52.613
It's not going to work.

00:02:53.865 --> 00:02:56.367
-Oh, yeah?
-And why is that, Granger?

00:02:56.451 --> 00:02:59.454
You see this? This is an Age Line.

00:02:59.620 --> 00:03:01.456
Dumbledore drew it himself.

00:03:01.539 --> 00:03:03.124
So?

00:03:04.625 --> 00:03:08.379
So a genius like Dumbledore
couldn't possibly be fooled...

00:03:08.463 --> 00:03:11.466
...by a dodge as pathetically dimwitted
as an Aging Potion.

00:03:11.549 --> 00:03:15.887
-But that's why it's so brilliant.
-Because it's so pathetically dimwitted.

00:03:17.555 --> 00:03:19.557
-Ready, Fred?
-Ready, George.

00:03:19.807 --> 00:03:21.559
BOTH:
Bottoms up.

00:03:25.063 --> 00:03:26.939
-Yes!
-Yes!

00:03:27.815 --> 00:03:29.442
Yeah!

00:03:30.485 --> 00:03:32.153
Yes!

00:03:32.487 --> 00:03:34.072
Ready?

00:03:37.450 --> 00:03:39.494
FRED AND GEORGE:
Yes!

00:03:40.703 --> 00:03:43.081
[BOTH YELLING]

00:03:47.960 --> 00:03:49.962
-You said!
-You said!

00:03:50.963 --> 00:03:54.425
-Oh, right, you want a piece of me?!
-I'll tear your ears off!

00:03:54.509 --> 00:03:57.095
-Now you're making me laugh.
-Take this! Come on!

00:03:57.303 --> 00:03:58.596
[CHANTING]
Fight! Fight! Fight!

00:04:03.726 --> 00:04:05.520
FRED:
We're "old school," eh?

00:04:05.603 --> 00:04:08.106
GEORGE:
Yeah, but you look older!

00:04:26.582 --> 00:04:28.709
[BELL TOLLING]

00:04:31.587 --> 00:04:33.714
[CHATTERING]

00:04:39.512 --> 00:04:42.140
DUMBLEDORE:
Sit down. Please.

00:04:45.309 --> 00:04:45.313
Now the moment
you've all been waiting for:

